# parrot — Environment Variables (i18n / l10n employee)
# Copy to .env and fill in your keys. .env is gitignored; this template is not.
#
# THE BLOCKING PATH NEEDS NONE OF THESE. parrot's merge gate (init → extract →
# check → a locale round-trips) is a pure file pipeline that runs $0 / offline /
# no-creds against the committed fixture (DECISIONS D15). Secrets appear ONLY at
# the TMS/MT seam, which is exercised by separately-gated, non-blocking golden
# legs. Provision a key only when you run that leg.

# --- Required (inherited platform key) ---------------------------------------

# Anthropic / Claude — the agent itself + direct-model MT for the sensitive 20%
# (set ZDR / no-train on the account when routing sensitive content — brain O16).
# Get at: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Optional: the Sandbox-component live render (NOT the merge gate) ---------

# E2B (Firecracker microVM) — boots the fixture app and renders /ar/ to prove
# dir="rtl" + a correct Arabic plural. The merge gate uses the ubuntu runner
# instead, so this is optional; absence does not block CI (DECISIONS D15).
# Get at: https://e2b.dev/dashboard
E2B_API_KEY=e2b_...

# --- Optional: the CI auto-PR translate loop ---------------------------------

# GitHub PAT — for the "translate in CI and open a PR" loop. The workflow needs
# `permissions: contents: write, pull-requests: write`, and the forked-PR case
# must be handled (the default GITHUB_TOKEN can't push from a fork — brain P22).
# Get at: https://github.com/settings/tokens
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=ghp_...

# --- Optional: the TMS / MT golden legs (separately gated, non-blocking) ------

# Lingo.dev — the AI-translate engine for the `parrot mt` golden leg.
# PIN THE CLI EXACTLY (lingo.dev@0.137.0, never ^): it is 0.x and releases almost
# daily; a ^-range pulls a breaking change overnight (brain P21). Its beta/next
# tags also LAG latest. Free/test tier is enough for the golden leg.
# Get at: https://lingo.dev (sign up, then API key)
# LINGODOTDEV_API_KEY=...

# Tolgee (OSS, self-host) — the `parrot tms` golden leg. Spin a local Tolgee dev
# container and point TOLGEE_API_URL at the local endpoint; self-host is free.
# Get at: https://tolgee.io (or run the docker container locally)
# TOLGEE_API_KEY=...
# TOLGEE_API_URL=http://localhost:8085

# --- Agent-operator hygiene (the manifest implies, the logger enforces) -------
#
# - Scope every TMS token tightly; never log API tokens or put them in URL query
#   strings — the Observability logger strips query strings to origin+pathname
#   before writing logs/runs.jsonl (brain agent-hygiene).
# - Crowdin CLI is a Java jar (needs a JRE) — provision one first, or prefer
#   Lokalise (Go) / Lingo.dev (Node) in a bare Node sandbox (brain P20).
